title Experiment 2 - map: the mutex baseline (2 threads, one counter)
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

* Exp 2: mutex baseline
** Question
*** What does the conventional std mutex cost when two threads share one counter?
** Setup
*** Two threads pinned to CPU 2 (core 1) and CPU 4 (core 2)
*** 5 M increments per thread, 11 trials after 1 warmup
*** Each thread does lock, plus plus, unlock on ONE shared counter
** Result (mean of 5 runs)
*** 24.55 ns per increment, slowest thread
*** 81.5 M increments per second total
*** 37 percent of thread CPU time spent in the kernel
*** About 60 voluntary context switches per trial
** Lesson
*** Correct, obvious, and slow under contention
*** Losers pay futex syscalls, not only sleeps
** Concepts to read first
*** Concept 04: how a mutex works
*** Concept 07: the cache line moves between cores
** Compared with
*** Experiment 3: the same loop with fetch_add
@endmindmap
